  <p class="credits-eyebrow">13 Times 3</p>
  <h1 id="credits-title">Credits</h1>
  <p class="credits-intro">The gallery is a place for our memories. Thank you to the artists whose work helps bring it to life.</p>
  <section class="credit-card" aria-labelledby="music-credit-title">
    <p class="credits-eyebrow">Gallery music</p>
    <h2 id="music-credit-title">“Resolutions”</h2>
    <p>Music by <a href="https://www.scottbuckley.com.au/library/resolutions/">Scott Buckley</a>.</p>
    <p>Licensed under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International</a>.</p>
    <p>The original MP3 was re-encoded at 128 kbps for web delivery. The music itself was not edited.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="credit-card" aria-labelledby="stage-music-credit-title">
    <p class="credits-eyebrow">Zephrine’s first stage · room 01</p>
    <h2 id="stage-music-credit-title">“Part of Your World”</h2>
    <p>Instrumental piano cover by <a href="https://soundcloud.com/bennymartinpianist/disney-the-little-mermaid-part-of-your-world-piano-instrumental-cover">Benny Martin</a>, streamed through his SoundCloud player. Music by Alan Menken, lyrics by Howard Ashman, from Disney’s <em>The Little Mermaid</em>.</p>
    <p>The recording is hosted by SoundCloud and is not included in the site’s downloads.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="credit-card" aria-labelledby="figure-credit-title">
    <p class="credits-eyebrow">Gallery figures</p>
    <h2 id="figure-credit-title">Storybook sculptures</h2>
    <p>The gallery combines authored dimensional hair, clothing and narrative poses with adapted facial and hand anatomy from the <a href="https://github.com/makehumancommunity/makehuman">MakeHuman graphical base and age morphs</a>, released under <a href="https://github.com/makehumancommunity/makehuman/blob/master/LICENSE.ASSETS.md">CC0</a>. Character proportions, materials and expressions are adapted for these memories.</p>
    <p>The hidden Ariel-inspired mermaid adapts the facial anatomy, body and hands of <a href="https://studio.blender.org/characters/rain/v3/">Rain Rig (CC) Blender Foundation | studio.blender.org</a>, under <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/">CC BY 4.0</a>. Her pose, materials and facial proportions are adapted, with newly authored hair, shells and tail following the requested 1989 Disney character design. Ariel belongs to Disney.</p>
    <p>Footwear adapts <a href="https://www.innerscene.com/tools/library/3d-parts/relaxed-walk-sam-3d-person-animated-732f1206">Innerscene’s “Relaxed walk — Sam”</a>, released under CC0. Earlier full-body studies of Sam and <a href="https://www.innerscene.com/tools/library/3d-parts/relaxed-walk-maya-3d-person-animated-2c6669a2">“Relaxed walk — Maya”</a> remain in the source archive.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="credit-card" aria-labelledby="fish-credit-title">
    <p class="credits-eyebrow">Aquarium sculpture</p>
    <h2 id="fish-credit-title">Painted fish</h2>
    <p>The detailed fish in the aquarium are adapted from the <a href="https://github.com/KhronosGroup/glTF-Sample-Assets/tree/main/Models/BarramundiFish">Khronos glTF Sample Assets BarramundiFish</a> model, released under CC0. Its texture was repainted for the gallery and the model was compressed for mobile viewing. The manta in the rear aquarium is an adapted, repainted <a href="https://quaternius.com/packs/animatedfish.html">CC0 manta model by Quaternius</a>.</p>
    <p>The four small reef-fish schools at the rear glass adapt <a href="https://github.com/BabylonJS/Assets/blob/master/meshes/fish.glb">Babylon.js Assets’ fish model</a>, licensed under <a href="https://github.com/BabylonJS/Assets/blob/master/LICENSE">Creative Commons Attribution 4.0</a>. Its animation was removed, its fish were arranged as separate static 3D groups, and its textures and geometry were compressed for this gallery.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="credit-card" aria-labelledby="tree-credit-title">
    <p class="credits-eyebrow">Street scenery</p>
    <h2 id="tree-credit-title">Outdoor shade trees</h2>
    <p>The job-search street, friendship garden, blue-car street, apple orchard, and Play Garden use an adapted <a href="https://poly.pizza/m/qZtx0AHhcy">tree by Quaternius</a>, released under CC0. Its scale, color, orientation, and mobile materials were changed for this gallery.</p>
  </section>
